tests:
  e2e:
    count: 2
    what: "tests/e2e_gate_truth.rs (1) - the epic e2e, composing all four fixes at one seam over a hermetic temp repo through the real xtask binary, the real pre-merge-commit hook and real git. A WU adds a component, retires its design per DEC-16 and cites it at the bytes the build read (P1/DEC-28, judged at its last state per DEC-29); the mr commit that lands its report reports landing, not error: (P2a); the report is link-checked red then green (P2b); the merge is refused for a signer this checkout does not list, naming the signer and the roster, then accepted for a listed one (P3). Each WU deferred this step in identical words; it is paid here. Regression proof: against an xtask built at the epic base 1c8d587 it reds at exactly P1 (does not resolve at the tip), P3 (no valid mr/v1 note) and P2b (ungoverned, not checked). tests/e2e_manual_review.rs (1) - E-NMWF epic e2e, re-run green after both files moved to the shared harness. xtask/tests/e2e_design_flow.rs (--features design-e2e, 5 tests, outside the 513-test default run) - W2 extended a_build_that_adds_a_surface_cites_the_design_it_read with the retired-design citation case."
  integration:
    count: 199
    what: "Every integration suite in the workspace, re-run green at this tip. This epic wrote or extended four: xtask/tests/mr.rs (58) - P2a and P3, including a commit that lands reporting success and no error, a first commit from an unborn HEAD, a signed note whose signer this checkout lists no key for naming the signer and the roster, and a genuine two-worktree test (worktree A signs, worktree B has no roster) proving the DEC-10 layout is the cause the message must name. xtask/tests/dod_gate.rs (82) - the citation predicate at the seam: green on the legal add-build-retire history, red on a fabricated path and on a blob no commit held, the DEC-29 retired-design artifact join, and the two design_scope tests that hold the design_artifacts_with de-duplication behaviour-preserving. xtask/tests/verify_doc.rs (16) - P2b: a dead relative href reds a governed doc and an ungoverned one, but not a draft, an archived doc or a docs/.archive/ link, plus a run over this repo own docs, itself now a test. tests/dod_hooks.rs (12) - the hook dispatch. Unchanged and re-run: tests/api.rs (11), tests/ca.rs (3), xtask/tests/doc_hooks.rs (8), xtask/tests/gate0_cache.rs (5), tests/worktree_setup_hook.rs (2), xtask/tests/ui.rs (2)."
  unit:
    count: 302
    what: "xtask/src (237) and src (65) library unit tests. This epic added coverage for the citation predicate widened through history, last_state and added_under, the retired-design artifact join, git_env/git_outcome error formatting and the commit verdict, the Authorisation enum three states, and the href resolver path handling."
suite: "513 tests green across 20 suites (cargo test --workspace --features hook-tests), unchanged across the review-fix refactor; the feature-gated design-e2e suite (5 tests) is additional. clippy --workspace --all-targets clean under pedantic with -D warnings."
counts_verified: "each figure read from cargo test output per suite at this tip, not from memory - a first draft of this note transposed dod_gate.rs (82) with the trawler unit suite (65) and understated the integration tier by 98, found by the epic review correctness finder"
review_fixes: "the epic tip carries three review fixes (987ca86): the two gate e2es share tests/common/gitrepo.rs, design_scope walks history once via design_artifacts_with, and an .eq(&false) became a negation. Their own coverage is the two design_scope tests plus both e2es re-run green, and the unit tier is waived for that commit - it removes a duplicate walk and extracts an existing harness, adding no behaviour a new unit test could assert."
